1. A variable
  type: A
  normal: x
2. A call with an unknown function
  type: A
  normal: (app f x)
3. An annotated identity
  type: (Pi A A)
  normal: (lambda #0)
4. Beta reduction
  type: A
  normal: x
5. A dependent identity
  type: (Pi * (Pi #0 #1))
  normal: (lambda (lambda #0))
6. Instantiate the dependent identity
  type: Nat
  normal: (succ (succ zero))
7. A type that computes
  type: Nat
  normal: zero
8. Normalization beneath a binder
  type: (Pi Nat Nat)
  normal: (lambda #0)
9. Natural-number elimination: 2 + 3
  type: Nat
  normal: (succ (succ (succ (succ (succ zero)))))
10. A length-indexed vector
  type: (Vec Nat (succ zero))
  normal: (cons Nat zero (succ (succ zero)) (nil Nat))
11. An index supplied by an earlier argument
  type: (Vec Nat (succ zero))
  normal: (cons Nat zero (succ (succ zero)) (nil Nat))
12. Dependent vector elimination
  type: (Vec Nat (succ zero))
  normal: (cons Nat zero (succ (succ zero)) (nil Nat))
13. Same length, zero head: result type Nat
  type: Nat
  normal: zero
14. Same length, successor head: result type Nat -> Nat
  type: (Pi Nat Nat)
  normal: (lambda #0)
15. Same length, unknown head: computation stays open
  type: (nat-elim (lambda *) Nat (lambda (lambda (Pi Nat Nat))) h)
  normal: (nat-elim (lambda (nat-elim (lambda *) Nat (lambda (lambda (Pi Nat Nat))) #0)) zero (lambda (lambda (lambda #0))) h)
